WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.920
Hey, Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:08.240
History is full of monsters: Adolf Hitler,
Joseph Stalin, and the bloke who invented

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.549
squirty cheese.

00:00:09.549 --> 00:00:14.749
, If it’s your life goal to be the world’s
biggest ‘see you next Tuesday’, there’s

00:00:14.749 --> 00:00:17.160
some pretty stiff competition.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:23.320
So when you earn yourself the epithet ‘the
Wickedest Man in the World’, you know you’ve

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:25.460
been a really naughty boy.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:31.339
But the man who did have that nickname, Aleister
Crowley, never cared too much about public

00:00:31.339 --> 00:00:32.339
opinion.

00:00:32.339 --> 00:00:38.920
The year was 1875 and Queen Victoria had wedged
her ample frame firmly onto the English throne

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:45.350
when, like many of history’s greatest villains,
Crowley was born in a rather smart townhouse

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.780
in Royal Leamington Spa.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:52.020
Considering the controversy he would court
throughout most of his adult life, Crowley

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:55.680
seems to have been a surprisingly normal kid.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.730
Having said that, in a nice bit of foreshadowing
it’s said his mother called him ‘the Beast’,

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:07.280
a nickname he would adopt in later life when
he started non-ironically referring to himself

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.960
as ‘the Great Beast 666’.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.920
Which sounds like the playstation network
username of a sexually frustrated teenager

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.240
to me, but I think people were quite impressed
at the time.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:25.240
Crowley’s father died of tongue cancer when
little Aleister was just 11 years old, and

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:30.159
it was this tragic event that set him on the
path to infamy.

00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:35.360
In the space of just a few short years, the
nice little boy from Leamington Spa had denounced

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:41.540
his religious beliefs, started causing trouble
at school, taken up smoking, and begun sleeping

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:47.060
with prostitutes, one of whom was generous
enough to give him gonorrhea along with the

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:48.240
services he’d paid for.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:55.980
It was to be the first of an impressive collection
of STDs Crowley would accumulate in his lifetime.

00:01:55.980 --> 00:02:01.420
Despite having become something of a rebel,
Crowley was an excellent student, and, at

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:05.430
the age of 20 he left home to study at Cambridge
University.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:10.190
As it is for many young people, uni was a
chance for Crowley to experiment.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:16.230
He switched courses from philosophy to English
literature, became an accomplished mountaineer,

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:20.790
and developed into such a strong chess player
he briefly considered going pro.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:27.670
He also conducted experiments of the sexual
variety, taking many partners of both sexes

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:31.660
and adding syphilis to his budding STD collection.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:37.130
Sex - especially of the weird variety - would
play a big part in the occultist activities

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:41.750
for which he would one day become famous - but
we’ll get to that later.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:46.320
He was a keen poet, a habit he kept up his
entire life.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:52.130
But his poems were, shall we say, a little
‘unusual’.

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:57.590
In his final year at Cambridge he published
a collection about, how can I put this without

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:03.910
getting demonetised - his, erm, ‘solo adventures.’

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:08.370
And just in case my meaning isn’t clear
enough, I can tell you he gave his new book

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:12.700
the rather charming title ‘White Stains.’

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:18.980
Which sounds pretty risque even today, so
you can imagine how people reacted in 1898

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.240
- not well.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:25.560
In the end he was forced to publish the collection
abroad for fear of persecution at home.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:31.560
Ultimately, it seems Crowley had little time
left over for trivial things like studying,

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.420
and he left university without obtaining a
degree.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:39.620
The good news was, he’d finally figured
out what he wanted to do with his life: Aleister

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:45.810
Crowley was going to dedicate himself to the
occult with the aim of becoming the world’s

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:48.040
most powerful magus.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.610
As you do.

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:55.320
To that end he became a member of the Hermetic
Order of the Golden Dawn, a secret society

00:03:55.320 --> 00:04:00.330
with an interest in the occult, metaphysics,
and the paranormal.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:04.300
The order had been founded by a couple of
freemasons ten years prior, and they were

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:08.860
known to spend their time studying astrology,
geomancy, and tarot cards.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:13.990
At this point you might be picturing some
kind of stereotypical secret society full

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:21.150
of aging white men dressing up in silly costumes
and taking part in arcane rituals, but in

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:23.990
this case you’d be… correct.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:27.180
Absolutely 100% correct.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:32.200
But this was a different time, and grown men
playing at wizards didn’t come with quite

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.410
the same stigma it does today.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:40.190
As a result, the Hermetic Order of the Golden
Dawn counted some important and celebrated

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:45.610
individuals among its number, including Bram
Stoker - he’d just published his seminal

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:51.660
novel ‘Dracula’ when Crowley joined the
order in 1898 - Irish poet W.B.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:56.890
Yeats, and Sir Arthur Conan Doyle, creator
of Sherlock Holmes.

00:04:56.890 --> 00:05:01.060
For the first time in his life, Crowley was
truly in his element.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:07.030
He took to his magic studies like Hermione
Granger on amphetamines, demonstrating the

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:12.130
kind of devotion he’d never brought to bear
at Cambridge, and he delighted in being around

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:14.390
like-minded individuals.

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:20.950
Well, I say ‘like minded’ - while the
Golden Dawn was everything Crowley had been

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:28.180
looking for, the Order did not, unfortunately,
feel quite the same way about Crowley.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:33.920
Many of the higher ups took their calling
as wizards and magi very seriously, and they

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:40.440
believed true power could only be attained
by those who abstained from drink, drugs,

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.660
and sex.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:47.550
Unfortunately, drink, drugs, and sex were
the three pillars upon which Crowley based

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:51.580
his entire existence, so clashes were inevitable.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:56.960
It’s rumoured he fell out with Yeats and
other important members of the order, and

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:01.870
when he was passed over for promotion to the
group’s inner circle, things went south

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:02.930
quickly.

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:07.950
Instead of taking the setback like a good
little wizard, Crowley went rogue, attempting

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:14.240
to seize control of one of the Golden Dawn’s
London temples known as the Vault of the Adepts.

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:20.950
Well I say ‘temple’ - it turns out the
Vault of the Adepts bears a striking resemblance

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:27.389
to your standard London terraced house, but
I guess ‘number 36 Blythe road’ didn’t

00:06:27.389 --> 00:06:29.900
sound quite mystical enough.

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:35.310
Unsurprisingly, this little stunt spelled
the end of Crowley’s career with the Hermetic

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:37.120
Order of the Golden Dawn.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:43.430
But his determination to become a great and
powerful wizard had not diminished - if anything,

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:46.550
getting the boot had lit a fire under his
arse.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:53.430
He began scouring the globe for ancient wisdom,
working his way through Mexico, the USA, India,

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:58.240
Japan, China, Hong Kong, Paris, Canada, and
Algeria.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:03.900
But it seems it was in Egypt he finally found
what he was looking for.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:08.740
Or should I say, what he was looking for found
him.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:14.420
Crowley had recently gotten married, and the
happy couple chose Cairo for their honeymoon.

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:19.360
Once safely in the honeymoon suite, Crowley
turned to his new bride and gave her a couple

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:25.480
of suggestive eyebrow raises - she knew exactly
what he wanted to do… turn the room into

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:29.340
a makeshift temple and start invoking Egyptian
deities.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:34.581
Ever the enigma, his honeymoon turned out
to be the only time Crowley didn’t have

00:07:34.581 --> 00:07:38.860
sex on the brain, though the couple must have
eventually gotten around to it because they

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:41.610
had their first child the following year.

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:46.990
We know Crowley was happy to become a father
because as a thank you to his wife for making

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:52.460
it all possible, he wrote her a charming collection
of pornographic poetry.

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:56.730
Because high brow porn is exactly what you
need when you’ve just squeezed a baby out

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:57.949
of your vagina.

00:07:57.949 --> 00:08:04.370
Anyway, after some vigorous, passionate, and
no doubt sweaty deity invoking in Cairo, a

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:10.550
spirit called Aiwass appeared and started
whispering in Crowley’s ear.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:16.870
Aiwass, as it turned out, was a messenger
of the God Horus, and it seems he had an awful

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:23.110
lot to say for himself, because once he started
talking he didn’t shut up for 3 days straight.

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:28.740
And this was no idle chit chat about the weather
or the frankly scandalous price of diesel

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:34.550
- when the 3 days were up, the messenger of
the Gods had dictated an entire book which

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:39.650
was to become the foundational text of a new
religion known as Thelema.

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:45.170
The text, which came to be known as ‘the
Book of the Law’, detailed how humanity

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:52.950
was about to enter a new era, and conveniently
enough it named Crowley as a prophet.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:59.690
It also outlined one supreme philosophy -- “Do
what thou wilt shall be the whole of the law”

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:04.050
– and this maxim became the cornerstone
of Thelema.

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:09.070
According to Crowley, life was all about the
pursuit of each person’s will, regardless

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:13.870
of popular opinion, law, or conventional ethics.

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:18.440
In other words, “Look after yourself and
screw everyone else.”

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:21.600
And he certainly seems to have practised what
he preached.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:27.610
For example, the following year he made an
ill-fated attempt to scale Kanchenjunga, the

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:33.200
world’s third highest mountain that was
at the time unclimbed and widely considered

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:36.540
the most dangerous peak on earth.

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:41.320
During the expedition, Crowley’s fellow
mountaineers eventually got sick of him being

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:46.630
reckless, weird, and a bit of a dick, and
they started making their way back down the

00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:49.060
mountain as night fell.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:54.150
This went against Crowley’s advice, and
sure enough, some of them were subsequently

00:09:54.150 --> 00:10:00.010
killed in an avalanche … but rather than
show concern for his fellow mountaineers,

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:06.360
or even settling for a simple “I told you
so”, Crowley is reported to have completely

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:12.540
ignored the survivors’ cries for help in
favour of chilling out in his tent.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:15.380
What a guy.

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:20.800
By 1920, Crowley was making plans to move
to the Italian island of Sicily to establish

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.370
a new headquarters for his religion.

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:29.210
It would become known as the Abbey of Thelema,
and a lot of freaky things went on there,

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:33.960
though almost all of them involved sex and
drugs in one form or another.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:40.020
You see, Crowley was a firm believer in something
he called ‘sex magick’, which he spelled

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:45.770
with a ‘K’ to make sure nobody mixed it
up with the boring old PG 13 magic you get

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:47.820
at children’s parties.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:54.260
Sex magick is an extremely complicated belief
system that requires many years of study to

00:10:54.260 --> 00:11:00.230
even begin to understand and a liftetime to
master, but I think I’ve managed to figure

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:05.250
out the gist: it’s a flimsy excuse to convince
people to have sex with you.

00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:10.760
Basically, if Crowley thought you were hot,
there was a good chance Aiwass, messenger

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:17.760
of Horus, was about to appear in a drug-fuelled
vision to demand an immediate orgy.

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:23.870
As ridiculous as this premise was, it seems
Crowley truly was a master of convincing men,

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:30.970
women, and - according to some rumours - animals
that his wand really was magical, because

00:11:30.970 --> 00:11:38.960
he practised his brand of sex magick all over
the world and with countless partners.

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:44.710
As for the drugs, Crowley is said to have
done so much cocaine at the abbey his nasal

00:11:44.710 --> 00:11:46.640
cavity began to erode.

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:51.050
It’s actually quite surprising he found
the time, considering how much heroin he was

00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:52.050
doing.

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:57.230
He was rather partial to a bit of opium, was
a big fan of hashish as an aid to mysticism,

00:11:57.230 --> 00:12:02.980
and was known to offer punch spiked with peyote
at get togethers with his followers just to

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:08.520
make sure everyone thought a bunch of weird
occult stuff had happened, even if all they’d

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:11.160
been doing was sitting on the sofa giggling.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:17.150
Anyway, it was all going swimmingly at the
Abbey until 1923, when one of Crowley’s

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:20.600
followers died after drinking water from a
polluted stream.

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:25.899
The man’s wife immediately returned to London
where she sold her story to the press.

00:12:25.899 --> 00:12:31.280
As well as the unfortunate death of her husband,
she spoke of terrible conditions at the Abbey

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:36.560
of the Thelemites, which sounded quite grand
but was actually a small cottage covered in

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:41.800
animal faeces, and of strange rituals performed
in the dead of night.

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:47.040
She also confessed she’d been forced to
drink the blood of a sacrificed cat on Crowley’s

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:53.270
orders, and that she and other Thelema acolytes
were required to cut themselves with razor

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:56.890
blades every time they used the pronoun ‘I’.

00:12:56.890 --> 00:13:02.399
And you thought being careful which pronouns
you used was a 21st century thing.

00:13:02.399 --> 00:13:07.660
The British press had a field day, and it
was here that Crowley was branded with the

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:12.730
title that would come to define him for the
rest of his days: “The wickedest man in

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:14.790
the world”.

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:23.170
The negative press was so bad that Mussolini,
in power in Italy at the time, had Crowley

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:25.130
forcibly deported.

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:28.740
You know you’re having a public relations
crisis when Mussonlini doesn’t want anything

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.110
to do with you.

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:33.620
Mind you, this wouldn’t be the only time
Crowley was thrown out of a country.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:38.730
He’d already been forced to leave India
after shooting two muggers, and in later life

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:44.200
he would be told to leave France on account
of his reputation for debauchery and occultism..

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:48.370
So yeah, he was about as popular in the queue
for immigration as COVID.

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:54.300
But the rough ride Crowley got in the British
press didn’t only stem from stories of death

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:59.720
and depravity at the Abbey of Thelema, nor
from the fact he was bisexual - homosexuality

00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:03.089
was illegal at the time - or his drug use.

00:14:03.089 --> 00:14:08.170
No, what really got Crowley in the bad books
was his support for the Germans during the

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:13.780
First World War, when he regularly wrote for
pro-German propagandist publications like

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:15.640
‘The Fatherland’.

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:21.529
As you can probably imagine, he was vilified
back home in blighty, but as it turned out,

00:14:21.529 --> 00:14:25.470
Crowley was actually one of the good guys
- at least in this case.

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:33.350
You see, he’d infiltrated German operations
so he could actively work against them, and

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:39.690
his overblown, hyperbolic rants in ‘The
Fatherland’ were carefully designed to make

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:42.320
the publication a laughing stock.

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:47.740
Aleister Crowley, grand magus and dark wizard,
was also working as a double agent for the

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:50.769
British Intelligence service in his spare
time.

00:14:50.769 --> 00:14:54.970
Perhaps considering all the crap he took in
the first World War, by the time the second

00:14:54.970 --> 00:14:59.920
World War broke out, Crowley had decided to
nail his colours firmly to the mast.

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:05.280
He branded Hitler a “Black Magician” and
wrote to the Naval Intelligence Division offering

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:08.310
his services in the fight against the Nazis.

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:13.830
On this occasion they declined, but Crowley
maintained close ties with a variety of writers

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:18.580
in the intelligence community, including Dennis
Wheatley, Roald Dahl, and Ian Fleming.

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:24.720
He must have had quite an impression on Ian
Fleming in particular, as the celbrated writer

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:31.130
not only based the James Bond villain “Le
Chiffre” on Crowley, but Crowley was also

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:37.279
Fleming’s first choice to interrogate occult-obsessed
Nazi Rudolph Hess when he was captured in

00:15:37.279 --> 00:15:38.279
Scotland.

00:15:38.279 --> 00:15:42.880
Despite not having much to do during the Second
World War, Crowley claimed to have made his

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:48.040
mark by coming up with the "V for Victory"
sign used by Winston Churchill, believing

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:52.130
it would be a powerful magical symbol to counteract
the swastika.

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:57.200
Whether or not he anticipated it’s modern
day usage - a handy way to say ‘eff you’

00:15:57.200 --> 00:16:00.610
when someone cuts you up on the motorway - is
unknown.

00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:09.400
Crowley eventually died in 1947 aged 72 in
poverty, obscurity, and no doubt significantly

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:13.220
less sexually active than he was in his prime.

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:19.320
After all, there can’t be many women, or
men, who are turned on by the “heroin-addicted-skeleton”

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:21.020
look.

00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:27.220
Despite his controversial life, Crowley’s
influence on occultism and pop culture can’t

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:28.220
be overstated.

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:35.200
His pet religion, Thelema, is still alive
today, and its followers believe Crowley to

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:40.120
have been a great prophet - just as Aiwass
claimed back in Egypt.

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:41.120
L. Ron.

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:44.579
Hubbard was once a dedicated Thelemite, and
it’s probably no coincidence he ended up

00:16:44.579 --> 00:16:50.810
following in his mentor’s footsteps in inventing
- sorry, I mean ‘discovering’ - his own

00:16:50.810 --> 00:16:52.220
religion: Scientology.

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:57.740
But it’s perhaps in the world of music that
Crowley is most fondly remembered, which probably

00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:03.110
shouldn’t come as a surprise - after all,
he may have been a black magician and an occultist,

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:10.339
but on a steady diet of sex, drugs, and, well,
more sex and drugs - he truly lived life like

00:17:10.339 --> 00:17:11.339
a rockstar.

00:17:11.339 --> 00:17:15.819
He became an icon for the hippie movement
of the 60s and 70s, and was namechecked in

00:17:15.819 --> 00:17:17.949
the work of some of the biggest bands in history.

00:17:17.949 --> 00:17:22.889
His mugshot made the cut on what might just
be the most famous album cover of all time

00:17:22.889 --> 00:17:24.230
- The Beatles’ Sgt.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:30.210
Pepper’s Lonely Hearts Club Band, and he’s
cropped up in songs by the likes of Led Zeppelin,

00:17:30.210 --> 00:17:33.710
David Bowie, Ozzy Osbourne, and the Red Hot
Chilli Peppers.

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:39.299
Zeppelin’s Robert Plant was so obsessed
with Crowley he even bought his old house.

00:17:39.299 --> 00:17:46.279
Whatever Crowley got up to during his highly
unconventional life, he not only had an indirect

00:17:46.279 --> 00:17:52.350
influence on those more anti-authoritarian
parts of pop culture -- the beat poets, rock

00:17:52.350 --> 00:17:56.850
n’ roll, and punk -- but also on things
like sexual liberation.

00:17:56.850 --> 00:18:02.999
He’s often accused of sexism, of course
-- between penning porn poems and telling

00:18:02.999 --> 00:18:08.749
women they had to sleep with him because his
made up God said so he wasn’t exactly a

00:18:08.749 --> 00:18:15.389
feminist -- but on the other hand, he also
advocated complete sexual freedom for both

00:18:15.389 --> 00:18:17.510
men and women.

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:23.810
Not only that, but he argued homosexual and
bisexual people should not be ashamed, or

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:29.769
afraid of who they were, and that they shouldn’t
have to “violate their own true nature”

00:18:29.769 --> 00:18:32.159
due to public opinion.

00:18:32.159 --> 00:18:38.590
For that, and many other reasons, he was way
ahead of his time.

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:44.129
Crowley once said “Certain actions produce
certain results”, and no matter what you

00:18:44.129 --> 00:18:49.730
might think about him, his actions produced
results which have shaped our world in a variety

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:51.049
of ways.

00:18:51.049 --> 00:18:59.130
In 2002, he was even voted number 73 in the
BBC’s list of “100 Greatest Britons,”

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:04.200
which surely would have enraged the tabloids
who gave him such a hard time during his life.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:08.109
So, was Aleister Crowley truly wicked?

00:19:08.109 --> 00:19:10.340
Well, kind of.

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:17.250
But as is often the case, the truth is a bit
more complicated than that.

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:25.650
Thanks for watching.

